    "case_summary": "A child weighing 30 kg, without any comorbidities and allergies, not taking any long-term medications, presented with erythematous, infiltrating, well-demarcated skin lesions located on the face, chest, abdomen, and limbs. The patient reported frequent contact with stray cats.\n\nErythematous, infiltrating, well-demarcated skin lesions were observed on the face, chest, abdomen, and limbs.\n\n{'Laboratory Tests': ['- Mycological culture yielded growth of Trichophyton mentagrophytes', '- Sequence analysis of internal transcribed spacer and D1/D2 domains of large-subunit rRNA gene', '- Initial blood tests showed:', '  * Erythrocyte sedimentation rate: 47 mm/h', '  * C-reactive protein: 25.8 mg/L', '  * White blood cell count: 15,390/uL', '  * Eosinophils: 11%', '  * IgE level: 7200 μg/L'], 'Imaging': {'Image Title': 'Clinical Details of the Inflammatory Lesions', 'Image Description': 'Images showing inflammatory lesions on the abdomen and forearm of the patient on admission and 12 hours after initiation of treatment'}}",
